{#-
  Pass-through chat template.

  The reward model's prompt is not a chat template's business. Its exact bytes --
  image placeholders, newlines, the empty assistant turn -- are part of the model
  (see the note in infer_vllm.py), so the client builds them with build_prompt()
  and ships the result as a single text part. This template's only job is to hand
  those bytes back unchanged.

  Why it has to exist at all: vLLM's /classify endpoint accepts images only in the
  chat-messages form, and the chat form always runs a template. A template that
  assembles the prompt from the parts would put the authority for those bytes in a
  jinja file, where a stray newline silently shifts every score. This one cannot:
  it emits text parts verbatim and ignores everything else, so whatever Python
  produced is exactly what the model sees.

  Images still reach the model: vLLM collects them from the image_url parts, in
  the order they appear in the message, and binds the Nth image to the Nth
  placeholder in the rendered prompt. So the client must list the original image
  first and the rendered image second, matching build_prompt()'s placeholder order.

  Requires --chat-template-content-format openai, so that message.content arrives
  as the list of parts rather than pre-flattened into a string.
-#}
{%- for message in messages -%}
{%- if message.content is string -%}
{{- message.content -}}
{%- else -%}
{%- for part in message.content -%}
{%- if part.type == 'text' -%}
{{- part.text -}}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
